---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout title="wdoc - The Document Format, Reimagined">
	<section class="w-full max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-20 sm:py-28 text-center">
		<div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-6">
			<h1
				class="text-gray-900 text-4xl sm:text-5xl md:text-6xl font-black leading-tight tracking-tighter"
			>
				The Document Format, Reimagined.
			</h1>
			<h2 class="text-gray-600 text-lg sm:text-xl font-normal leading-normal max-w-3xl">
				Developer-friendly, interactive, and secure. The modern replacement for PDF.
			</h2>
			<!-- <button
				class="flex min-w-[84px] max-w-[480px] cursor-pointer items-center justify-center overflow-hidden rounded-lg h-12 px-6 bg-primary text-white text-base font-bold leading-normal tracking-[0.015em] hover:bg-primary/90 transition-colors"
			>
				<span class="truncate">Explore the Spec</span>
			</button> -->
		</div>
	</section>
	<section class="w-full max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16 sm:py-24">
		<div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-12 lg:gap-24 items-center">
			<div class="flex flex-col gap-6">
				<div class="flex items-center gap-4">
					<div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-primary/10 flex items-center justify-center">
						<span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary">psychology</span>
					</div>
					<h3
						class="text-gray-900 tracking-light text-3xl font-bold leading-tight sm:text-4xl"
					>
						Seamlessly Parsed by AI
					</h3>
				</div>
				<p class="text-gray-600 text-base font-normal leading-relaxed">
					The structured, non-binary nature of wdoc makes it incredibly easy for AI and
					scripts to read, understand, and extract data without complex parsing.
				</p>
				<!-- <button
					class="flex min-w-[84px] max-w-[480px] cursor-pointer items-center justify-center overflow-hidden rounded-lg h-12 px-5 bg-primary text-white text-base font-bold leading-normal tracking-[0.015em] w-fit hover:bg-primary/90 transition-colors"
				>
					<span class="truncate">Learn More</span>
				</button> -->
			</div>
			<div
				class="w-full bg-gray-100 rounded-xl p-2 aspect-video flex items-center justify-center border border-gray-200"
			>
				<img
					class="w-full h-full object-cover rounded-lg"
					data-alt="basic wdoc index.html example"
					src="/assets/code.png"
				/>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
	<section class="w-full max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16 sm:py-24">
		<div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-12 lg:gap-24 items-center">
			<div
				class="w-full bg-gray-100 rounded-xl p-2 aspect-video flex items-center justify-center lg:order-last border border-gray-200"
			>
				<img
					class="w-full h-full object-cover rounded-lg"
					data-alt="An interactive mockup of a form within a document frame. Users can see fields being filled and an 'Attach ID' button that simulates a file upload."
					src="/assets/form.png"
				/>
			</div>
			<div class="flex flex-col gap-6">
				<div class="flex items-center gap-4">
					<div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-primary/10 flex items-center justify-center">
						<span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary">edit_document</span>
					</div>
					<h3
						class="text-gray-900 tracking-light text-3xl font-bold leading-tight sm:text-4xl"
					>
						Forms that Work for You
					</h3>
				</div>
				<p class="text-gray-600 text-base font-normal leading-relaxed">
					Fill forms directly within the document. Answers are saved locally, and you can
					even embed critical attachments like ID cards or supporting documents.
				</p>
				<!-- <button
					class="flex min-w-[84px] max-w-[480px] cursor-pointer items-center justify-center overflow-hidden rounded-lg h-12 px-5 bg-primary text-white text-base font-bold leading-normal tracking-[0.015em] w-fit hover:bg-primary/90 transition-colors"
				>
					<span class="truncate">See it in Action</span>
				</button> -->
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
	<section class="w-full max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16 sm:py-24">
		<div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-12 lg:gap-24 items-center">
			<div class="flex flex-col gap-6">
				<div class="flex items-center gap-4">
					<div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-primary/10 flex items-center justify-center">
						<span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary">verified_user</span>
					</div>
					<h3
						class="text-gray-900 tracking-light text-3xl font-bold leading-tight sm:text-4xl"
					>
						Simple, Secure, Verifiable Signing
					</h3>
				</div>
				<p class="text-gray-600 text-base font-normal leading-relaxed">
					Utilize the built-in digital signature process, complete with email validation, to
					ensure every signature is secure and verifiable.
				</p>
				<!-- <button
					class="flex min-w-[84px] max-w-[480px] cursor-pointer items-center justify-center overflow-hidden rounded-lg h-12 px-5 bg-primary text-white text-base font-bold leading-normal tracking-[0.015em] w-fit hover:bg-primary/90 transition-colors"
				>
					<span class="truncate">Learn More</span>
				</button> -->
			</div>
			<div
				class="w-full bg-gray-100 rounded-xl p-2 aspect-video flex items-center justify-center border border-gray-200"
			>
				<img
					class="w-full h-full object-cover rounded-lg"
					data-alt="A three-step infographic: 1. A finger clicking a 'Sign' button. 2. A mock email validation checkmark. 3. The document showing a 'Signed &amp; Verified' stamp."
					src="/assets/secure.png"
				/>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
	<section class="w-full max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16 sm:py-24">
		<div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-12 lg:gap-24 items-center">
			<div
				class="w-full bg-gray-100 rounded-xl p-2 aspect-video flex items-center justify-center lg:order-last border border-gray-200"
			>
				<img
					class="w-full h-full object-cover rounded-lg"
					data-alt="A visual of a main document file with smaller icons for XLSX, PPTX, and MD files flowing into it, showing the container concept."
					src="/assets/container.png"
				/>
			</div>
			<div class="flex flex-col gap-6">
				<div class="flex items-center gap-4">
					<div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-primary/10 flex items-center justify-center">
						<span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary">inventory_2</span>
					</div>
					<h3
						class="text-gray-900 tracking-light text-3xl font-bold leading-tight sm:text-4xl"
					>
						More Than Just a Document
					</h3>
				</div>
				<p class="text-gray-600 text-base font-normal leading-relaxed">
					wdoc acts as a container, holding related files like spreadsheets, presentations,
					or technical documentation, keeping all your project assets in one place.
				</p>
				<!-- <button
					class="flex min-w-[84px] max-w-[480px] cursor-pointer items-center justify-center overflow-hidden rounded-lg h-12 px-5 bg-primary text-white text-base font-bold leading-normal tracking-[0.015em] w-fit hover:bg-primary/90 transition-colors"
				>
					<span class="truncate">Explore Use Cases</span>
				</button> -->
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
  <section id="version-history" class="w-full max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16 sm:py-24">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-12 lg:gap-24 items-center">
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-6">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-primary/10 flex items-center justify-center">
            <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary">history</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-gray-900 text-3xl font-bold leading-tight sm:text-4xl">Your document. Every version.</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="text-gray-600 text-base leading-relaxed">
          Git history travels inside your .wdoc file. Keep a timeline of saved versions,
          recover working drafts, and restore earlier content without losing what came after it.
        </p>
        <p class="text-gray-600 text-base leading-relaxed">
          While you edit, changes are autosaved every 30 seconds when the browser permits it.
          Save merges your draft into the published version and keeps the intermediate steps.
          A linked local file is updated directly.
        </p>
        <p class="text-gray-600 text-base leading-relaxed">
          Bring another copy into a visual comparison, combine independent changes, and choose
          how conflicts are resolved. Original signatures stay with their exact versions;
          the merged draft is ready for a new signature. Your documents stay local.
        </p>
        <a class="text-primary font-semibold hover:underline" href="https://app.wdoc.info">Try version history in the editor →</a>
      </div>
      <figure class="rounded-xl bg-gray-100 p-3 border border-gray-200">
        <img src="/assets/version-history.png" alt="The wdoc editor comparing two project proposals and previewing a merged document with the updated budget and delivery date" class="w-full h-auto rounded-lg" loading="lazy" width="1094" height="913" />
        <figcaption class="mt-3 text-sm text-gray-600">Visual merging in the wdoc editor. No remote Git service required.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
          